WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.415
The Barths left the coffee shop and headed to the park.

2
00:00:04.416 --> 00:00:07.208
They saw many children there.

3
00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:08.973
Some were at the playground.

4
00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:11.297
Others were playing baseball.

5
00:00:11.298 --> 00:00:14.452
"Oh, she's flying a kite!"

6
00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:17.979
Jane pointed to a little girl with a red kite.

7
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.835
"Is that your daughter?" a woman sitting on a bench asked.

8
00:00:22.836 --> 00:00:26.848
"Excuse me?" Jane was confused.

9
00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:31.340
"That girl, is she yours?" the woman asked again.

10
00:00:31.341 --> 00:00:35.337
"Of course not!" Jane shouted hotly.

11
00:00:35.338 --> 00:00:38.589
"I'm too young to have children!"

12
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:43.427
She gave the woman a nasty stare and walked off.

13
00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:47.460
The woman looked at Jane strangely.

14
00:00:47.461 --> 00:00:50.926
"What did that woman say to you?" asked Cy.

15
00:00:50.927 --> 00:00:55.527
"She thought I was a mother!" Jane was still upset.

16
00:00:55.528 --> 00:00:58.696
"But Jane," Panther said gently.

17
00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:00.944
"You are grown-up now."

18
00:01:00.945 --> 00:01:05.062
Before Jane could answer, they heard familiar sounds.

19
00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:07.647
"It's the ice cream truck!"

20
00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:10.116
Bobby jumped up and down.

21
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:16.396
"Since coffee was so yucky," grinned Cy, "we deserve something sweet!"

22
00:01:16.397 --> 00:01:20.334
The grown-up Barths raced across the park.

23
00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:24.455
Being bigger and faster, they passed all the little children.

24
00:01:24.456 --> 00:01:27.483
They got to the ice cream truck first.

25
00:01:27.484 --> 00:01:33.325
"Double caramel chocolate fudge, please," said Bobby, rubbing his hands.

26
00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.717
"Excuse me," the driver said coldly.

27
00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:39.623
"Maybe the children should go first."

28
00:01:39.624 --> 00:01:43.553
He pointed to the line of children behind the Barths.

29
00:01:43.554 --> 00:01:47.706
"I got here first," Bobby replied stubbornly.

30
00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.268
Some parents made rude remarks.

31
00:01:50.269 --> 00:01:53.552
"That grown man should be ashamed."

32
00:01:53.553 --> 00:01:57.153
"He's acting like a child!"

33
00:01:57.154 --> 00:02:00.442
The driver shrugged and gave Bobby his ice cream.

34
00:02:00.443 --> 00:02:03.911
"I'll have a strawberry twist," Panther said.

35
00:02:03.912 --> 00:02:07.767
"Do you all work together?" the driver asked her.

36
00:02:07.768 --> 00:02:09.565
"No, we're family,"

37
00:02:09.566 --> 00:02:13.114
she replied as she took the ice cream from him.

38
00:02:13.115 --> 00:02:16.186
"Is today your day off?" he asked.

39
00:02:16.187 --> 00:02:19.864
"What do you mean?" Panther asked in return.

40
00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:21.774
"You're not working today?"

41
00:02:21.775 --> 00:02:24.851
the man said in an irritated voice.

42
00:02:24.852 --> 00:02:28.357
"Work? I don't have a job," she said.

43
00:02:28.358 --> 00:02:30.086
"None of us do."

44
00:02:30.087 --> 00:02:33.489
The man looked at her with a nasty expression.

45
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:37.179
"You should be ashamed of yourself!" he said.

46
00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.104
"All grown-ups work hard to make money. But you─"

47
00:02:41.105 --> 00:02:43.447
He pointed to each of the Barths.

48
00:02:43.449 --> 00:02:46.772
"─you only want ice cream."

49
00:02:46.773 --> 00:02:50.545
Suddenly the ice cream no longer seemed inviting.

50
00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:55.241
The Barths looked around and saw angry faces.

51
00:02:55.242 --> 00:02:58.541
"Maybe we should go," said Cy.

52
00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:01.771
They hung their heads and turned away.

53
00:03:01.772 --> 00:03:04.621
"Why are people so mean?"

54
00:03:04.622 --> 00:03:07.835
Jane asked after they found a quiet bench.

55
00:03:07.836 --> 00:03:11.640
"Because we acted like children," replied Panther.

56
00:03:11.641 --> 00:03:15.360
"But we are children," argued Jane.

57
00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.867
"Not today, Jane!

58
00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:20.478
We're grown-ups today, remember?" said Cy.

59
00:03:20.479 --> 00:03:25.635
"Everyone sees us as grown-ups who act like children."

60
00:03:25.636 --> 00:03:27.937
The Barth kids were silent.

61
00:03:27.938 --> 00:03:30.473
They watched other children playing.

62
00:03:30.474 --> 00:03:33.871
"They look so happy," said Bobby.

63
00:03:33.872 --> 00:03:37.136
"I wish I could ride a bike, too."

64
00:03:37.137 --> 00:03:41.777
"I thought being a grown-up would be fun," Jane sniffed.

65
00:03:41.778 --> 00:03:45.154
"I didn't know it would be so hard."

66
00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:48.586
The Barths sat at the bench for a while.

67
00:03:48.587 --> 00:03:51.303
They didn't know what else to do.

68
00:03:51.304 --> 00:03:53.698
Then Cy looked at his watch.

69
00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:57.187
"Let's go back to Aunt Martha's," he said.

70
00:03:57.188 --> 00:04:00.194
"We can hide until the sun sets."

71
00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:05.162
"I can't walk in these shoes anymore," cried Jane.

72
00:04:05.163 --> 00:04:07.697
She threw her heels on the ground.

73
00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:11.417
"Okay, Jane," Cy said, "I'll carry you."

74
00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:14.425
Jane climbed onto Cy's back.

75
00:04:14.426 --> 00:04:18.114
"Whoa! You're heavy!" he gasped.

76
00:04:18.115 --> 00:04:22.683
But like a good brother, he carried his sister through the park.

77
00:04:22.684 --> 00:04:26.052
People passing by stopped and stared.

78
00:04:26.053 --> 00:04:31.110
"Oh, my!" they muttered. "What are they doing?"

79
00:04:31.111 --> 00:04:36.256
"They should be ashamed of themselves."

